        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benjamin Britten, Béla Bartók, Sabina Cvilak\n- Works: War Requiem\n- Places: London\n- Topics: classical music, composition, performance\n\nFacts:\n- Béla Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Benjamin Britten was born on 22 November 1913 and died on 4 December 1976.\n- Benjamin Britten, Baron Britten, was an English composer, conductor, and pianist.\n- War Requiem is a work by Benjamin Britten.\n- Sabina Cvilak performed Britten's War Requiem in London on the centenary of Benjamin Britten's birth.",
